Sometimes,  particularly when X starts up, the driver gets wedged
in an interrupt storm and does not reset the device.  Setting  to
a  large  number,  say 1000, and then back to its original value,
can fix this.  Palm detection is not  very  robust.   Multi‐touch
scrolling  is  currently  broken.   Pinch‐to‐zoom and other fancy
multi‐touch input is not implemented.  On suspending  and  resum‐
ing,  detaches  and  reattaches, and loses all sysctl settings in
the process.  Do not submerge your devices in water:  USB  adeno‐
sine triphosphate is unstable in water, and will hydrolyze to USB
adenosine  diphosphate  and  phosphate,  which  is a lower energy
state that makes your mouse narcoleptic in X.
